-- Q3320: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both amounts are reported as revenue and expense on the government-wide statements","The new bonds create a liability while the old bonds remain until legally defeased with a deferred amount recognized","No adjustment is needed because the fund statements already reflect the correct treatment","The old bonds are immediately removed and replaced by the new bonds on the statement of net position"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 65, advance refunding requires the government-wide statements to record the new bonds as a long-term liability while the old bonds remain until legally defeased. The difference between the reacquisition price and net carrying amount is recognized as a deferred outflow or inflow of resources.
Wrong (A): Bond proceeds and escrow payments are not reported as revenue and expense; they are liability transactions on the government-wide statements.
Wrong (C): An adjustment is required because governmental funds report proceeds/payments as other financing sources/uses, which differs from the accrual treatment.
Wrong (D): The old bonds remain on the books until legal defeasance occurs, not upon issuance of new bonds.$EXPL$
