-- Q3323: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Add the increase in supplies inventory to convert to full accrual basis","Subtract the decrease in supplies inventory to reflect consumption","Add the net increase in supplies inventory because government-wide statements record supplies as assets until consumed","No adjustment is needed because supplies are treated the same under both measurement focuses"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 78, when governmental funds use the purchases method, supplies are expensed when purchased. Government-wide statements use the consumption method, expensing supplies when used. An increase in inventory means fewer supplies were consumed than purchased, so the excess must be added back.
Wrong (A): This is partially correct but incomplete; the adjustment specifically reflects the net change under the consumption method, not merely the increase.
Wrong (B): Subtracting a decrease would be the wrong direction; a decrease in inventory means more was consumed, which is already captured.
Wrong (D): The two measurement focuses treat supplies differently, requiring reconciliation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3323;

-- Q3324: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Amortized over the bond term using the effective interest method","Reported as other financing sources in the period of issuance","Not recorded in the governmental fund financial statements","Reported as deferred revenue until the bonds mature"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraphs 77-79, bond premiums received at issuance are reported as other financing sources in governmental funds. The current financial resources measurement focus does not require amortization at the fund level.
Wrong (A): Amortization occurs on the government-wide statements under the economic resources measurement focus, not in governmental funds.
Wrong (C): Bond premiums are recorded in governmental funds as other financing sources alongside the face amount of the bonds.
Wrong (D): A bond premium is not deferred revenue; it represents additional proceeds from issuing bonds above par value.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3324;

-- Q3327: Interfund Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A reciprocal exchange of goods or services between two funds","A one-way flow of resources without repayment or direct benefit","A temporary loan requiring repayment between governmental funds","A payment for services rendered by one fund to another fund"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, an interfund transfer is a one-way movement of resources between funds without a corresponding return flow of assets, services, or repayment. Transfers are reported as other financing sources in the receiving fund and other financing uses in the providing fund.
Wrong (A): A reciprocal exchange describes an interfund service provided and used, not a transfer.
Wrong (C): A temporary loan between funds is an interfund advance or borrowing that requires repayment, not a transfer.
Wrong (D): Payments for services rendered are classified as interfund services provided and used under GASB 34.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3327;

-- Q3329: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both are classified as transfers because all interfund resource flows are nonreciprocal movements between funds","The IT payment is a nonoperating transfer while the road funding is an operating expenditure for capital assets","Both are reported as revenues and expenses because GASB treats all interfund activity as quasi-external transactions","The IT payment is revenue and expense (a genuine service exchange at market rates) while the road transfer is an other financing source/use (a nonreciprocal resource movement)"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): GASB Statement No. 34 distinguishes interfund services provided and used from interfund transfers based on whether a genuine exchange occurs. The IT services transaction involves a real service at approximate market value, so it is reported as revenue in the General Fund and expense in the Enterprise Fund. The road transfer is nonreciprocal with no exchange of goods or services, reported as other financing sources/uses.
Wrong (A): Interfund services provided and used are specifically distinguished from transfers under GASB 34.
Wrong (B): This reverses the classification of both transactions.
Wrong (C): Only genuine exchanges receive revenue/expense treatment, not all interfund activity.$EXPL$
