-- Q3333: Interfund Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A transfer out in the General Fund and a transfer in for Capital Projects","Revenue in the Capital Projects Fund and an expenditure in the General Fund","A receivable in the General Fund and a payable in the Capital Projects Fund","An expenditure in the General Fund with no corresponding entry in Capital Projects"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112a, an interfund loan creates reciprocal receivable and payable balances: a ''due from other funds'' in the lending General Fund and a ''due to other funds'' in the borrowing Capital Projects Fund. These are balance sheet items that do not affect revenues or expenditures.
Wrong (A): Transfers represent permanent one-way resource movements; loans require repayment and are not transfers.
Wrong (B): Interfund loans do not generate revenue or expenditures; they create only balance sheet items.
Wrong (D): Both funds must record the transaction; the borrowing fund records a payable.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3333;

-- Q3335: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An interfund transfer reported as other financing sources and uses","An interfund reimbursement correcting a prior misallocation of costs","An interfund service provided and used, recorded as revenue and expenditure","An interfund loan creating reciprocal receivable and payable balances"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112, when a proprietary fund provides services to other government funds at its normal billing rate, the transaction is classified as an interfund service provided and used. The enterprise fund recognizes revenue and the general fund records an expenditure, mirroring external transaction treatment.
Wrong (A): Transfers are nonreciprocal one-way resource movements; this is a genuine exchange of services at market rates.
Wrong (B): Reimbursements correct costs charged to the wrong fund, not routine service billings.
Wrong (D): Loans create balance sheet items with repayment terms; this is an exchange of services for payment.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3335;

-- Q3337: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Eliminated during the government-wide consolidation process","Reported as an expense of governmental activities on the statement","Reported as revenue of business-type activities on the statement","Reported separately as transfers in and transfers out on the statement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 61, transfers between governmental activities and business-type activities are not eliminated on the government-wide statements because they cross activity boundaries. The transfer appears as a transfer out in governmental activities and a transfer in for business-type activities.
Wrong (A): Elimination applies to interfund activity within the same activity type, not cross-activity transfers.
Wrong (B): Transfers are not expenses; they are reported separately below the expense line on the statement of activities.
Wrong (C): Transfers are not revenue; they are reported in a separate transfers line item.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3337;

-- Q3339: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
