-- Q3340: Interfund Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An interfund transfer moving resources permanently between the two funds","Writing off the overpayment as a loss in the General Fund","An interfund reimbursement from the Special Revenue Fund to the General Fund","Recognizing additional revenue in the General Fund to offset the overpayment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112, an interfund reimbursement restores costs initially charged to the wrong fund. The Special Revenue Fund reimburses the General Fund, reducing the General Fund''s expenditures while recording the cost in the Special Revenue Fund where it properly belongs.
Wrong (A): Transfers are permanent resource reallocations, not corrections of misallocated expenditures.
Wrong (B): Writing off the amount would leave the expenditure in the wrong fund and misstate both funds'' financial statements.
