WHERE id = 3340;

-- Q3341: Interfund Transactions [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Eliminated to the extent it creates a profit margin in the fund","Left as reported because internal charges reflect actual billing rates","Reported as miscellaneous revenue on the government-wide statements","Charged against fund balance as a prior period adjustment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 61, internal service fund charges exceeding actual cost create internal profits that must be eliminated on the government-wide financial statements. The 10% markup inflates both departmental expenses and internal service fund revenues, which does not represent an arm''s-length external transaction.
Wrong (B): While appropriate for fund-level accounting, internal markups must be removed at the government-wide level to present actual cost of operations.
Wrong (C): Internal overcharges are not miscellaneous revenue; they are artificial profits that distort government-wide reporting.
Wrong (D): The overcharge is not a prior period adjustment; it is an ongoing elimination entry for government-wide consolidation.$EXPL$
