-- Q3375: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Can designate retroactively to the original transaction date","Cannot apply hedge accounting and must report all fair value changes in earnings","Must wait until the next fiscal year to formally designate the hedge","Can apply hedge accounting after a mandatory 30-day waiting period"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815, hedge accounting requires formal designation and documentation at inception of the hedge relationship. If the entity fails to designate at inception, hedge accounting cannot be applied retroactively, and all changes in the derivative''s fair value are recognized in current earnings.
Wrong (A): ASC 815 does not permit retroactive hedge designation; documentation must exist at inception.
Wrong (C): There is no fiscal year waiting period; the entity simply cannot apply hedge accounting to that particular relationship.
Wrong (D): ASC 815 contains no 30-day waiting period provision; designation must occur at inception or not at all.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3375;

-- Q3377: Derivatives and Hedging [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Reclassified to earnings immediately upon discontinuation of the hedge","Written off against retained earnings as a cumulative effect adjustment","Reversed against the derivative''s current fair value on the balance sheet","Retained in AOCI and reclassified to earnings when the forecasted transaction occurs"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 815, when a cash flow hedge is discontinued because it is no longer effective but the forecasted transaction is still expected to occur, amounts in AOCI remain there. They are reclassified to earnings in the same period the forecasted transaction affects earnings.
Wrong (A): Immediate reclassification occurs only if the forecasted transaction is no longer expected to occur, not merely when hedge effectiveness is lost.
Wrong (B): AOCI amounts are not written off against retained earnings; they follow the forecasted transaction into earnings.
Wrong (C): Reversing against the derivative''s fair value conflates the hedged item with the hedging instrument.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3377;

-- Q3380: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Long-term liabilities reported only on the government-wide statements","Short-term liabilities reported in the governmental fund receiving proceeds","Off-balance-sheet financing disclosed only in the notes to statements","Deferred revenue recognized until the taxes are actually collected"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Tax anticipation notes are short-term borrowings expected to be repaid from tax collections within the current fiscal period. Because they mature within the current period, they meet the current financial resources measurement focus and are reported as fund liabilities in governmental funds.
